package Physics.Tests

use Libraries.Game.Collision.LocalCollisionPoints3D

/*
The flat box as item A. The normal points up, from the triangle toward
the box, and the points on B are on the triangle's thickened surface.

Unless a test says otherwise, the triangle is a large one lying flat
at height 0, from MakeLargeTriangle, with the usual margin of 0.04, so
its thickened surface is at 0.04. The box is 0.5 on each side for
collisions (see RunBox), with no rotation, and the triangle is item A.
A box whose center is at 0.28 has its bottom at 0.03, so it sinks 0.01
into the surface.
*/
class BoxTriangleIsItemATest is PhysicsTest
    on create
        SetName("Box and triangle: box as item A")
    end

    action Run
        LocalCollisionPoints3D points = RunBox(MakeLargeTriangle(0.04), MakeTransform(0, 0.28, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0), true)
        CheckWhole("box as item A: four contacts", points:GetPointCount(), 4)
        CheckAllContacts("box as item A", points, 0, 1, 0, -0.01)
        CheckWhole("box as item A: point on the triangle", CountContactsNear(points, 0.25, 0.04, 0.25), 1)
    end
end
